Reimplement desktop app with Tauri 2, reusing master's Elm codebase

Replaces the Electron main process with a Rust backend (src-tauri/):
- Doc/home window lifecycle, native menus with recent documents
- File I/O with swap files and temp backups (.gkw/.gko/.md)
- Per-document undo history as JSON stores under app data
- Recent documents + per-file settings store
- txt/json export; docx export via pandoc; JSON import via Elm worker
- File associations, single-instance file-open, save-changes dialogs

Frontend glue in src/tauri/ ports src/electron/renderer.js and home.js
to Tauri invoke/events, including a browser-compatible sha1 commit-tree
port. Built by esbuild-tauri.mjs into tauri-web/ (Elm + esbuild +
tailwind + static assets).

Elm changes to bring the desktop targets up to master's shared modules:
- Electron.elm ported to opaque Page.Doc API (opaqueUpdate/opaqueIncoming,
  Doc.History for version history, data ownership moved to wrapper)
- Restore SavedToFile/ClickedExport/DataSaved in Page.Doc.Incoming
- Restore viewFullscreenButtonsDesktop in Doc.Fullscreen
- Expose UI.Header.viewExportMenu; fix ShortcutsModal viewShortcuts arity

